      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T21:19:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On TextBigO/64 specifically: TextBigO runs markDirty(); layout(300); in a tight loop on 64 code units 0..63, so every iteration after the first is a ~4us cache hit that only copies the cached runs/clusters and breaks one short line. With 0 unresolved codepoints, fUnresolvedCodepoints is nullptr, so shared_ptr assignment does a single null check (no atomic refcount increment). Replacing std::unordered_set (56 bytes) with std::shared_ptr (16 bytes) shrinks ParagraphImpl by 40 bytes and shifts the cache-line alignment of fLines right after it.",
